# BuildKit reads THIS file (named after the Dockerfile it sits next to) instead
# of a root `.dockerignore`, which the monorepo does not otherwise have. Without
# it, stage 1 of `Dockerfile` — which needs the whole workspace so `turbo prune`
# can see every `package.json` and compute the dependency graph — would also
# copy every app's `node_modules`, build cache and git history into the image.
#
# What is NOT excluded is deliberate: every workspace's source and `package.json`
# stay in, because `turbo prune @montaj/worker-media` is the thing that works out
# which of them actually matter, and doing that filtering here by hand is a
# second, hand-maintained copy of the dependency graph turbo already has.

**/node_modules
**/.git
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/.next*
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.venv
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.hypothesis
**/__pycache__
**/.env
**/.env.*
opensource-clipping-main/
postiz-app-main/
scratch/
